## Summary
The article discusses Armenia's pro-European Union prime minister targeting his former rival, former President Robert Kocharyan. Kocharyan and his son have been detained as part of a corruption investigation, highlighting political tensions and anti-corruption efforts in Armenia.

## Key Points
- Armenia's prime minister is aligned with the European Union.
- Former President Robert Kocharyan is a primary target of the current administration.
- Kocharyan and his son have been detained in a corruption probe.
- This action indicates political rivalries and enforcement of anti-corruption measures in Armenia.


